  "replay": [
    "Create a fresh chmod 0700 directory outside the tracked tree with source-tree/ and tmp/ subdirectories.",
    "At the pinned revision, use git archive --output for the two lists in pins, extracting both archives into source-tree/. Apply the overlay from the private directory with git apply --check then git apply.",
    "Copy the locked Hex cache to <scratch>/.hex and Mix archives to <scratch>/.mix/archives. Under source-tree/hosted run env -i HOME=<scratch> TMPDIR=<scratch>/tmp PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@17/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin LC_ALL=C MIX_ENV=test HEX_OFFLINE=1 ERL_FLAGS='+S 4:4' mix deps.get --check-locked, then mix compile --warnings-as-errors with the same environment.",
    "Copy the pinned SwiftPM swift-crypto and swift-asn1 bare repositories to <scratch>/swift-cache/repositories/ using their cache directory names. Run python3.14 -B owned.py from the private directory to build the stock CLI. Its Git transport accepts only file access.",
    "Run python3.14 -B replay.py once in that same private directory. It records per-command group absence and loopback rebinds. On ordinary completion remove the private directory after copying the compact receipt. Preserve its exact namespace if HOLD.jsonl is present."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Test-compiled ordinary Phoenix/Bandit browser fixture with a synthetic identity provider and loopback SCRAM PostgreSQL. The PostgreSQL connections did not use production TLS.",
    "The stock CLI writer targets the configured default target. The iOS and Android writes ran after independent API application starts on the same restored database; the read restart served both registered targets.",
    "No billing service, payment credentials, live provider, or customer dependency. Delivery readback ends at verified assignment, manifest and payload; no installation, activation, device, or production evidence.",
    "The custodian directly checked each recorded top-level process group. Synchronous CLI clients ran as descendants of the restore ExUnit command; their four successful exits were asserted by ExUnit. Initial Hex dependency and hosted compilation commands were observed complete through the exec transport before the supervised campaign."
  ],
